WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.100
What would get an actor banned from a&nbsp;
talk show? Well, don't touch that dial:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.840
we're about to count down a list of banned&nbsp;
actors and get into just what went awry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.020
from inebriation to interjection to altercation.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:20.100
In the 1990s, Vivica A. Fox was a major star. She&nbsp;
hasn't been part of a blockbuster hit in decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.780
but she's more than capable of a comeback&nbsp;
at any time — except on Jimmy Kimmel Live,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:28.200
following a bitter feud with its&nbsp;
host that got her banned as a guest.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.160
It all started in 2005 when Fox&nbsp;
appeared on Kimmel's late-night&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.900
show. During his usual snappy, joke-laden&nbsp;
introduction of the former Soul Food star,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.640
Kimmel made a crack about one of Fox's&nbsp;
close friends, The View host Star Jones.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.080
In an awkward and uncomfortable interview&nbsp;
Fox pushed back at Kimmel's insults.

00:00:46.301 --> 00:00:50.141
"You know, I'm a ride or die chick.&nbsp;
You not gonna talk about my sister."

00:00:50.141 --> 00:00:54.240
In an attempt to salvage the interview,&nbsp;
Kimmel argued that jokes go both ways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.020
but Fox wasn't pleased, and ultimately&nbsp;
walked off the stage midway through.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:03.540
Speaking to Bravo host Andy Cohen nearly a&nbsp;
decade later, Kimmel said he banned Fox from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:08.460
the show after that and even suggested she may&nbsp;
have been using drugs during her appearance. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:12.957
didn't sit well with Fox for obvious reasons,&nbsp;
and the two have been at odds ever since.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.960
In the mid-2000s, Dax Shepard was an up-and-comer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.868
appearing in slacker comedies like Employee of&nbsp;
the Month, Idiocracy, and Let's Go to Prison.

00:01:21.279 --> 00:01:22.119
"Guilty as hell."

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:26.340
He finally cleaned himself up after a struggle&nbsp;
with substance abuse. But before he got sober,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:29.280
Shepard was banned from one of&nbsp;
the biggest late-night shows.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:34.920
During an appearance on the podcast The Pursuit of&nbsp;
Healthiness, Shepard talked about a 2004 interview&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.660
he did on Late Night With Conan O'Brien while&nbsp;
he was at a particularly low point, admitting,

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:44.700
"I had done the pre-interview in a blackout, and&nbsp;
I woke up to the hotel security shaking me awake."

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.860
After being rushed to the set of the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.980
a disastrous interview with&nbsp;
host Conan O'Brien ensued.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:53.984
"You know what? I would never&nbsp;
have me back if I were you."

00:01:53.984 --> 00:01:54.960
Shepard recalled,

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.280
"I don't know what he's talking about. I can&nbsp;
tell he's queuing me up for stories I've told,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.840
but I don't know any of the stories. So, I'm&nbsp;
just doing what I can to be funny out there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:08.520
and I am a mess. So I was banned from that&nbsp;
show for some years until I got sober."

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.917
Since getting clean, the actor has appeared&nbsp;
on Conan's TBS show many more times.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:17.460
As Star Trek's Captain James T. Kirk,&nbsp;
William Shatner went boldly where no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:21.960
man had gone before. But while Kirk could&nbsp;
defeat alien entities, vengeful madmen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:26.580
and Klingon warlords, he met his match in&nbsp;
the form of Tonight Show host Johnny Carson.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.140
Tonight Show guests were banned for giving&nbsp;
controversial interviews, being belligerent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:35.460
and combative, or even for being under the&nbsp;
influence. But Shatner was apparently given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:40.980
the heave-ho for not being able to shut up. He&nbsp;
came clean in his 2011 memoir Shatner Rules:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:45.180
Your Guide to Understanding the Shatnerverse&nbsp;
and the World at Large. In a particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:48.780
lively passage about his adventures&nbsp;
in talk show land, Shatner writes,

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:52.980
"I was even banned from Carson after&nbsp;
a mid-1980s appearance where I talked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.460
too much and monopolized our&nbsp;
discussion. It seems some of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.640
these talk show hosts prefer to be&nbsp;
the ones who get all the laughs."

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.300
Shatner returned to the series&nbsp;
years later, after Carson retired.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:09.840
British icon Hugh Grant was nominated for best&nbsp;
actor Emmys in 2020 and 2019 for his roles in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:15.300
prestige dramas A Very English Scandal and The&nbsp;
Undoing. But, while his recent success on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.500
small screen has garnered him accolades, there&nbsp;
was a time when he was a bigger name on the big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.880
screen, particularly after his leading role in&nbsp;
the classic rom-com Four Weddings and a Funeral.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:28.560
However, despite his worldwide celebrity,&nbsp;
Grant was banned from The Daily Show in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:33.780
2001. As reported by Third Beat at the time,&nbsp;
then-host Jon Stewart appeared at a charity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:38.160
fundraiser and talked about banning Grant.&nbsp;
He described a frustrating appearance during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.460
which Grant complained about the clip&nbsp;
they were using from his recent film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:45.420
describing him as the worst guest&nbsp;
they'd ever had. Stewart said,

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.340
"He's giving everyone s--- the whole time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:50.520
and he's a big pain in the ass. [...]&nbsp;
And we've had dictators on the show."

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:54.780
In 2012, Grant actually admitted he was&nbsp;
wrong in a Twitter confession, writing,

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:58.380
"Turns out my inner crab got the&nbsp;
better of me. [...] Unforgivable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.780
J Stewart correct to give me kicking."

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:05.820
In the 1980s, pop star Madonna was known&nbsp;
for her controversial hits such as "Like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:10.020
a Virgin" and "Papa Don't Preach" but it&nbsp;
wasn't her music that got her on British&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:14.580
talk show host Piers Morgan's blacklist.&nbsp;
In a 2011 interview with Access Hollywood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:18.360
Morgan made it clear that his acrimony&nbsp;
towards the Queen of Pop was personal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.480
and described what he called "a&nbsp;
series of crimes" against him.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.700
Morgan told host Billy Bush,

00:04:23.899 --> 00:04:27.439
"A few things have gone down&nbsp;
between Madonna and I. She knows."

00:04:27.439 --> 00:04:30.660
Morgan claims his animosity&nbsp;
began years ago, explaining,

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:34.021
"There was a bread roll throwing&nbsp;
incident in London in the mid '90s;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.021 --> 00:04:37.980
there was an incident at [...] the Cannes Film&nbsp;
Festival involving a photographer and a bodyguard;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:42.060
there's been an incident involving a pub owned&nbsp;
by her [...] [ex-] husband, Guy Ritchie."

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:46.500
Apparently, Morgan hasn't forgiven&nbsp;
the pop star. In 2023, he tweeted:

00:04:46.699 --> 00:04:51.079
"I think Madonna's become the biggest&nbsp;
cringe-making fiasco in world entertainment."

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:54.480
Piers Morgan seems to have a problem&nbsp;
with almost everyone in Hollywood.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:59.340
Another target of his ire is Frasier star&nbsp;
Kelsey Grammer, though this time it might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:03.420
be understandable. While his feuds with&nbsp;
other celebs stem from personal dislike,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:08.580
Morgan's reason for banning Grammer has its roots&nbsp;
in an appearance the sitcom star made in 2012.

00:05:09.024 --> 00:05:10.500
"I didn't like it."

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:14.520
Grammer was to appear on Piers Morgan&nbsp;
Live but wasn't happy when the show used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:19.080
an image of his ex-wife Camille Donatacci&nbsp;
in the opening. Grammer and Donatacci had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:23.820
a troubled relationship and divorced in 2010.&nbsp;
While he'd been booked as the featured guest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:26.340
when the time came, Grammer was a no-show.

00:05:27.759 --> 00:05:28.959
"This isn't gonna work."

00:05:29.201 --> 00:05:30.204
Morgan tweeted,

00:05:30.204 --> 00:05:32.760
"I like Kelsey Grammer personally, but this was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:37.200
a shockingly unprofessional thing to do. I&nbsp;
wasn't even going to mention his ex-wife!"

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:41.446
As a result of the incident, Morgan&nbsp;
publicly banned Grammer from the show.

00:05:41.446 --> 00:05:45.660
Late-night talk shows have spawned plenty&nbsp;
of famous fights. Back in the '80s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:49.200
then-host of The Tonight Show Johnny&nbsp;
Carson famously held a grudge against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:55.140
comedian Joan Rivers. Rivers first appeared&nbsp;
on The Tonight Show in 1965. In the 1980s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:59.460
she became the de facto host any time&nbsp;
Johnny Carson needed a night off. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:02.940
things were never the same after Rivers&nbsp;
became the host of her own talk show.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:06.420
In a CNN segment aired after her death in 2014,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:09.420
Rivers recalled telling Carson&nbsp;
about her new show, saying,

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:13.320
"Fox came with this amazing offer&nbsp;
and we took it. And he was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:16.020
first one I called. And, as I said, he hung up."

00:06:16.139 --> 00:06:19.139
Apparently, an unhappy Carson&nbsp;
ended their friendship.

00:06:19.139 --> 00:06:23.160
From then on, Rivers was banned from&nbsp;
The Tonight Show, a prohibition that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:28.980
continued even when Jay Leno took over. In a 2014&nbsp;
interview with Access Hollywood, Leno explained,

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:31.860
"I didn't want to do it while&nbsp;
Johnny was alive out of respect."

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:36.000
Leno's successor, Jimmy Fallon, ended&nbsp;
the ban in time for Rivers to make a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.400
triumphant final appearance just before her death.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:43.500
While there are plenty of celebrities and actors&nbsp;
who were banned by hosts of a single talk show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:47.820
controversial comedian Kathy Griffin says&nbsp;
she's been banned from several. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:50.760
she's proud of the reasons she's been&nbsp;
prohibited from the likes of The Talk.

00:06:50.859 --> 00:06:52.959
"I crossed the line? What line?"

00:06:52.959 --> 00:06:56.580
In 2022, Griffin told her Twitter&nbsp;
followers she'd been banned thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.580 --> 00:07:00.840
to her vocal criticism of CBS chairman&nbsp;
Les Moonves, throwing her weight behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:05.520
allegations of sexual assault that had dogged&nbsp;
him for years. She was also embargoed from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.540
David Letterman's show in the 1990s and&nbsp;
remains persona non grata at The View.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:14.640
But that's still not the end of it. Griffin's&nbsp;
ongoing battle with Ellen DeGeneres left her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:19.620
uninvited, if not formally banned. Sparked&nbsp;
by Griffin's defense of Joan Rivers, the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:24.000
wound up nearly at each other's throats,&nbsp;
with vitriol apparently hurled both ways.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:28.680
The Walking Dead's chopper-riding,&nbsp;
crossbow-wielding Daryl Dixon is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:32.340
one of the few characters to live&nbsp;
through the entire series. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:37.740
he's set for a spin-off. Yet the actor who plays&nbsp;
him, Norman Reedus, has at least one nemesis:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:42.480
radio talk show host Howard Stern, who Reedus&nbsp;
claims refuses to have him on his show.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:46.740
On Jon Bernthal's podcast Real&nbsp;
Ones, Reedus, a huge Stern fan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:51.060
lamented the ban and claimed not to know&nbsp;
what was behind it. According to Bernthal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:54.600
Stern's dislike of Reedus likely stems&nbsp;
from an encounter the actor had with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:58.800
the talk show host's wife, Beth Ostrosky,&nbsp;
who happens to be a big fan of the actor.

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:04.140
Stern suggested there was some kind of flirtation&nbsp;
between Ostrosky and Reedus, but Reedus denies it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:09.660
By Reedus' account, he only chatted with Stern's&nbsp;
wife over their mutual love of cats. But Bernthal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:14.372
thinks Stern's obsessed with their meeting, and&nbsp;
as a result, wants nothing to do with Reedus.

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:17.880
Dax Shepard isn't the only guest&nbsp;
banned by host Conan O'Brien.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:21.540
Comedian and Howard Stern colleague&nbsp;
Artie Lange was banned because Conan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:25.020
and network executives were concerned&nbsp;
he might be relapsing into drug abuse.

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:28.500
Lange was confused at being denied&nbsp;
a guest spot on Late Night after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:30.900
two previous appearances, telling the Daily News,

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:35.520
"I am sober. I can't be a third guest? I&nbsp;
mean, I'm not asking to bump George Clooney."

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:41.880
But the ban didn't last forever. In 2012, Lange&nbsp;
appeared as a guest on Conan on TBS, where O'Brien&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:45.480
made clear that past treatment of Lange was&nbsp;
out of nothing but concern for his health.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:51.237
The late comedian Gilbert Gottfried was known for&nbsp;
his wacky, off-the-wall persona and silly voice.

00:08:51.237 --> 00:08:54.420
"I like to get the Internet&nbsp;
to hate me right away."

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:56.850
"Well, we're well on our way tonight, Gilbert."

00:08:56.850 --> 00:09:01.680
He played iconic roles in Aladdin and Problem&nbsp;
Child, but his younger fans weren't aware of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:06.840
filthy side. Gottfried actually had an entire&nbsp;
comedy album titled Dirty Jokes. But it wasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:11.400
his vulgarity that got him banned by Howard&nbsp;
Stern. In fact, it's still a bit of a mystery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:15.780
why Gottfried's longtime friend Howard Stern&nbsp;
refused to have him on as a guest for years.

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:20.760
None other than Artie Lange confirmed that&nbsp;
Gottfried was banned, announcing it on Twitter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:25.620
in 2018. Lange suggested it may have been&nbsp;
because Gottfried wasn't a popular draw,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:29.880
while others believe it started in 2010,&nbsp;
when Gottfried jokingly spit in a couple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:34.920
of cupcakes meant for Stern show staffers after&nbsp;
his interview, then dared crew members to eat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:39.660
them. Gottfried passed away in 2022, so,&nbsp;
unless Stern is willing to open up about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:44.100
just what happened between them, this is&nbsp;
one ban that may forever remain a mystery.

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:47.700
It seems that Tonight Show host&nbsp;
Johnny Carson had a tendency&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:51.300
to hold a grudge. In addition to&nbsp;
Joan Rivers and William Shatner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:55.080
Everybody Loves Raymond star Brad&nbsp;
Garrett also got on his bad side.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:57.240
Garrett was banned from The Tonight Show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:00.540
after defying orders to alter the&nbsp;
material in his stand-up routine.

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:05.280
"I told Tommy Newsom I had sperm&nbsp;
bigger than him. Not funny."

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:06.360
"But true."

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:07.200
"But true."

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.600
As a result, he was never invited back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:12.720
proving there was a steep price&nbsp;
to pay for crossing Johnny Carson.

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:17.400
That's not the only controversy Garrett&nbsp;
stirred up on the show. According to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:21.360
book When the Balls Drop: How I Learned to&nbsp;
Get Real and Embrace Life's Second Half,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:25.860
Garrett defied house orders and did an&nbsp;
impression of guest host Bill Cosby that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:29.340
drew laughs from the audience but&nbsp;
a cold stare from Cosby himself.

